tive of hematological malignancy", "Paraneoplastic syndrome: Neurological features (ataxia, visual changes) might suggest paraneoplastic processes, but primary hematological findings dominate the presentation", "Metabolic decompensation: Diabetes could explain some symptoms, but labs show normoglycemia and no acute metabolic derangement"], "alarm_features": ["Unintentional weight loss", "Night sweats", "Low-grade fever", "Leukocytosis with blasts"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.2088806828923175, "posterior": 0.15550578600941076, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Blasts in peripheral blood are not characteristic of multiple myeloma (B4), providing strong support for myeloid neoplasms (B1) instead."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.002, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The lack of lymphoid markers in blast morphology and presence of myeloid features make lymphoid neoplasm (B2) less likely than myeloid (B1)."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.34282578177021505, "posterior": 0.2443332731095256, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Subacute 